WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.390
Set your calculator to radians.

2
00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.190
Type one, and press equals.

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:08.880
Now type cos of Ans, and press equals.

4
00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:11.460
Nought point five four nought three.

5
00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:12.980
Press equals again.

6
00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:14.130
And again.

7
00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.530
The outputs jump up, then down, then up.

8
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.360
Then the screen freezes.

9
00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.140
Do the outputs shrink to nothing?

10
00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:22.610
Jump about forever?

11
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.130
Where does it end?

12
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.180
In this mission, you'll
see this as an iteration:

13
00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:32.700
each output becomes the next input,
x n plus one equals g of x n.

14
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.110
You'll rearrange equations
ready to iterate,

15
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.250
and run them from a starting value.

16
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.090
And you'll check a root
by a change of sign.

17
00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.590
Your mission: find where pressing
cos of Ans again and again ends up.
